# The client attached the block and published at least one frame, and that frame
# produced damage. A file-transport client would report damaged_px=0 here.
~compositor: ext=\S+ launched=1

# Three published rectangles (initial frame, edited line, status label) with a
# total well under two full frames: a keystroke batch repaints the line and the
# label, not everything in between. bg>0 proves the desktop pass was skipped for
# rectangles fully covered by the window.
~compositor: ext rects=[3-9][0-9]* damaged_px=(3[0-9]{5}|4[0-3][0-9]{4}) bg=[1-9][0-9]* last=[0-9]{1,3}x[0-9]{1,3}@

# Neither the PWIN pixel file nor the event file is created: frames and input
# both travel through the shared block.
!_comp_

!compositor: FAIL
